=== layout: one-plus-two-panels

# Biochemistry Lecture

@left

- [*Structure explains function*]{color=blue}
  - We go into great detail on protein structure, enzyme function, and other macromolecules.
  - Protein purification, separation methods, and enzyme kinetics.
- [*Protein-structure assignments*]{color=blue}
  - Make images in UCSF Chimera and explain what they show.
  - Connect a molecule's structure with what it does.

@top-right

![Upper-Level Introductory Biochemistry textbook cover](repo:evergreen/assets/upcoming_courses/biochemistry_textbook_cover.png)

@bottom-right

BCHM 355-20 / 455-20, [Spring 2027]{color=blue}; 3 credits\
Thursdays, 2:00-4:30 p.m.; SCH 612\
January 19-May 10 (Session 1)\
CRNs: 355 = 24780; 455 = 24781

