=== layout: one-panel

# Biochemistry Lab

@body

- BCHM 356-20 / 456-20, [Spring 2027]{color=blue}; 3 credits
  - Tuesdays, 10:00 a.m.-1:55 p.m.; SCH 550
  - Face-to-face, Schaumburg; January 19-May 10 (Session 1)
  - CRNs: BCHM 356 = 22046; BCHM 456 = 22049
- [*Less structured and more independent study-like*]{color=blue}
  - Enzyme assays and kinetics: measure reaction rates and interpret the data.
  - Isolation and analysis of biological macromolecules.
  - Explore protein sequence, structure, and folding using molecular software and databases.
- [*Experimental design and analysis*]{color=blue}
  - Data collection, graphs, and interpretation are part of the lab work.

=== layout: one-panel

# Cellular and Molecular Biology

@body

- BIOL 301, [Spring 2027]{color=blue}
  - [My teaching assignment is not confirmed yet.]{color=red}
- [*The chemistry of life*]{color=blue}
  - Biological molecules and how they work in cells.
  - Cell structure, membranes, transport, and communication.
  - Cellular energy: respiration and photosynthesis.
  - DNA, gene expression, and regulation.
- [*Lecture, laboratory, and discussion*]{color=blue}

=== layout: one-panel

# Biology and Ethics in Film

@body

- BIOL 383-20 / 483-20, [Summer 2027]{color=purple}; 3 credits
  - Tuesdays/Thursdays, 6-9 p.m., over Zoom
  - July 6-August 9 (Session D)
  - CRNs: BIOL 383 = 32156; BIOL 483 = 32157
- [*Watch a feature film, then discuss*]{color=purple}
  - Explore its biology, science, and ethical questions.
  - Give quick post-film "hot takes" and make a group movie-review podcast.
- [*Weekly journal prompts*]{color=purple}
  - Make a case, include your opinions, and think critically.
  - Most of the grade is a weekly writing prompt; getting it done is key.
